1
00:02:31,069 --> 00:02:41,069
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,069 --> 00:02:45,069
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,069 --> 00:02:52,069
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,069 --> 00:03:00,069
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:03:00,069 --> 00:03:09,069
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,069 --> 00:03:13,069
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:16,069 --> 00:03:24,069
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:24,069 --> 00:03:32,069
The Fishman Pirates, led by Horty Jones and assisted by Vander Decken, plot to overthrow King Neptune.

9
00:03:32,069 --> 00:03:39,069
It's not long before the Straw Hats get pulled into the conflict and find themselves in the midst of an all-out war.

10
00:03:39,069 --> 00:03:42,069
Perhaps!

11
00:03:42,069 --> 00:03:47,069
But even if you could stop it, you would still have to go through me first.

12
00:03:47,069 --> 00:03:51,069
And if memory serves, that didn't work out so well last time.

13
00:03:51,069 --> 00:03:57,069
Horty! What's happened to you?

14
00:03:57,069 --> 00:04:02,069
There are people living in the Fishman District who were once your allies!

15
00:04:02,069 --> 00:04:06,069
What you're doing doesn't benefit anyone, not even you!

16
00:04:06,069 --> 00:04:10,069
Why can't you see that, Horty?

17
00:04:14,069 --> 00:04:16,069
Is there something I don't know?

18
00:04:16,069 --> 00:04:21,069
Or is your hatred so deep that you've abandoned your sense of reason entirely?

19
00:04:21,069 --> 00:04:24,069
Tell me the cause of this madness!

20
00:04:24,069 --> 00:04:25,069
Did humans attack you?

21
00:04:25,069 --> 00:04:28,069
Did they torment you in some untold manner?

22
00:04:28,069 --> 00:04:30,069
Did they kill your friends?

23
00:04:30,069 --> 00:04:32,069
Did they hurt your family?

24
00:04:32,069 --> 00:04:34,069
Did they take something you hold dear?

25
00:04:34,069 --> 00:04:36,069
Answer me, dammit!

26
00:04:36,069 --> 00:04:39,069
What did humans do to you that was so unforgivable?

27
00:04:39,069 --> 00:04:40,069
Why?

28
00:04:40,069 --> 00:04:43,069
What in this world could inspire such cruelty?

29
00:04:43,069 --> 00:05:03,069
This is the air tank. We've met before, remember?

30
00:05:03,069 --> 00:05:05,069
Oh, yeah, hey guys!

31
00:05:05,069 --> 00:05:08,069
We've been listening to what's happening out there.

32
00:05:08,069 --> 00:05:11,069
And we can see the Noah hurtling toward the island.

33
00:05:11,069 --> 00:05:14,069
We've begun making the preparations as we've discussed.

34
00:05:14,069 --> 00:05:17,069
Don't make it more complicated! Just go for it, okay?

35
00:05:17,069 --> 00:05:20,069
And Luffy, everyone here is counting on you.

36
00:05:21,069 --> 00:05:25,069
Can you hear me, Straw Hat?

37
00:05:25,069 --> 00:05:53,069
Please, listen. He spoke earlier and… It's clear now. Gordy is… Gordy! Gordy?

38
00:05:53,069 --> 00:05:56,069
Yes! Gordy!

39
00:05:56,069 --> 00:05:57,069
Yes!

40
00:05:57,069 --> 00:06:03,069
J-j-j-j-j-j-j-j-j-j-J-j-j-j-j-j-j-j-j-j-j-j-jj-j-j-j-j.

41
00:06:03,069 --> 00:06:10,889
Shocking fact, the true identity of Horty.

42
00:06:20,889 --> 00:06:25,209
Earlier that day, before the Noah began its descent on the island,

43
00:06:33,069 --> 00:06:35,069
it was a very good one.

44
00:06:35,069 --> 00:06:36,069
Whoa!

45
00:06:36,069 --> 00:06:37,069
Whoa!

46
00:06:37,069 --> 00:06:38,069
Whoa!

47
00:06:42,069 --> 00:06:43,069
Whoa!

48
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:44,069
Whoa!

49
00:06:44,069 --> 00:06:45,069
Whoa!

50
00:06:45,069 --> 00:06:46,069
Whoa!

51
00:06:46,069 --> 00:06:47,069
Whoa!

52
00:06:47,069 --> 00:06:48,069
Whoa!

53
00:06:48,069 --> 00:06:49,069
Whoa!

54
00:06:49,069 --> 00:06:50,069
Whoa!

55
00:06:50,069 --> 00:06:51,069
Whoa!

56
00:06:51,069 --> 00:06:53,069
Oh, my knee!

57
00:06:53,069 --> 00:06:54,069
Oh!

58
00:06:54,069 --> 00:06:55,069
Oh!

59
00:06:55,069 --> 00:06:56,069
Oh!

60
00:06:56,069 --> 00:06:59,069
You jerk!

61
00:06:59,069 --> 00:07:02,069
You really made me mad, you know that?

62
00:07:02,069 --> 00:07:05,069
Oh!

63
00:07:05,069 --> 00:07:08,069
This is what you get!

64
00:07:08,069 --> 00:07:10,069
Intimidation!

65
00:07:10,069 --> 00:07:12,069
Megabuck!

66
00:07:21,069 --> 00:07:23,069
Come on, it was big enough already!

67
00:07:33,069 --> 00:07:35,069
Am I supposed to be impressed?

68
00:07:35,069 --> 00:07:39,069
Well, you're surprised, right?

69
00:07:39,069 --> 00:07:42,069
I'm a Tiger Blowfish Fishman!

70
00:07:42,069 --> 00:07:43,069
Scary, huh?

71
00:07:43,069 --> 00:07:45,069
Not really.

72
00:07:45,069 --> 00:07:47,069
Kinda curious why you're talking like that, though.

73
00:07:47,069 --> 00:07:50,069
Cause I'll deflate if I keep my mouth open, you idiot!

74
00:07:50,069 --> 00:07:51,069
I could...

75
00:07:52,069 --> 00:07:54,069
The Kraken is still way bigger than you.

76
00:07:54,069 --> 00:07:55,069
Oh, yeah?

77
00:07:55,069 --> 00:07:56,069
Fine!

78
00:07:56,069 --> 00:07:57,069
Then how about this?

79
00:07:57,069 --> 00:07:59,069
Blue House D!

80
00:07:59,069 --> 00:08:00,069
How annoying!

81
00:08:00,069 --> 00:08:02,069
Don't crush me, dammit!

82
00:08:02,069 --> 00:08:03,069
Stop it!

83
00:08:03,069 --> 00:08:04,069
What is zooming?

84
00:08:04,069 --> 00:08:05,069
We're on your side!

85
00:08:05,069 --> 00:08:07,069
You're squashing all of us!

86
00:08:07,069 --> 00:08:09,069
Still a shrimp compared to the Kraken.

87
00:08:09,069 --> 00:08:10,069
Impossible!

88
00:08:10,069 --> 00:08:12,069
Blue House D!

89
00:08:12,069 --> 00:08:15,069
Good job, you moron!

90
00:08:15,069 --> 00:08:20,069
We have come, your majesty!

91
00:08:20,069 --> 00:08:25,069
Are you all right down there?

92
00:08:25,069 --> 00:08:28,069
I'm so sorry, my king!

93
00:08:28,069 --> 00:08:32,069
We should have been able to protect you, and we failed!

94
00:08:32,069 --> 00:08:34,069
We're pathetic, worthless vassals!

95
00:08:34,069 --> 00:08:35,669
Worthless vassals!

96
00:08:35,689 --> 00:08:36,629
Never mind that.

97
00:08:37,009 --> 00:08:39,269
More importantly, did you see the Noah?

98
00:08:39,569 --> 00:08:40,069
Yes.

99
00:08:41,029 --> 00:08:43,829
Tragic that it's been moved under such circumstances.

100
00:08:44,569 --> 00:08:45,709
Curse you, Deccan.

101
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:49,749
I never thought you would sink so low as to destroy your own island.

102
00:08:50,229 --> 00:08:51,709
And your own people.

103
00:08:52,269 --> 00:08:53,329
Trust me, Your Majesty.

104
00:08:53,329 --> 00:08:55,549
We were just as shocked as you were.

105
00:08:55,869 --> 00:08:58,529
We even tried to order an island-wide evacuation.

106
00:08:58,989 --> 00:09:02,709
But those new fishmen pirate bastards are blocking any transmission.

107
00:09:04,069 --> 00:09:08,509
Even worse, we haven't been able to make contact with the bloodguards out at sea.

108
00:09:09,929 --> 00:09:11,729
Prepare to shoot the bubble now!

109
00:09:11,869 --> 00:09:12,149
Hurry!

110
00:09:16,789 --> 00:09:17,349
See?

111
00:09:18,149 --> 00:09:19,469
They won't pick up.

112
00:09:19,969 --> 00:09:23,249
You need to get the king out of here in some place safe now.

113
00:09:23,249 --> 00:09:23,829
No.

114
00:09:24,189 --> 00:09:24,429
Huh?

115
00:09:25,609 --> 00:09:28,409
I'm waiting right here for the princes.

116
00:09:34,069 --> 00:09:39,389
What in blazes?

117
00:09:42,689 --> 00:09:43,989
Someone explain this.

118
00:09:44,049 --> 00:09:44,749
What's happening?

119
00:09:45,289 --> 00:09:48,129
Like, for starters, where did all these damn pirates come from?

120
00:09:48,609 --> 00:09:49,289
Well, sir?

121
00:09:49,289 --> 00:09:58,549
The straw hats are on our side?

122
00:10:02,089 --> 00:10:02,649
Jimbe.

123
00:10:03,949 --> 00:10:05,169
And the princess?

124
00:10:06,529 --> 00:10:07,209
Forty.

125
00:10:08,029 --> 00:10:08,589
Deccan.

126
00:10:09,109 --> 00:10:11,089
So that's what happened.

127
00:10:11,089 --> 00:10:15,809
All right, men.

128
00:10:16,289 --> 00:10:18,009
Everything is clear to me now.

129
00:10:19,689 --> 00:10:21,529
All of you, to the plaza.

130
00:10:22,029 --> 00:10:22,929
Follow Jimbe.

131
00:10:23,389 --> 00:10:24,969
Back up the straw hats.

132
00:10:26,729 --> 00:10:29,529
If the straw hats can handle the more powerful fighters,

133
00:10:30,009 --> 00:10:31,849
our men can suppress the others.

134
00:10:32,549 --> 00:10:33,349
It's insane.

135
00:10:33,789 --> 00:10:36,549
We tried to arrest them, yet they're fighting to save our island.

136
00:10:37,129 --> 00:10:39,229
We should be ashamed for not trusting them.

137
00:10:39,229 --> 00:10:44,029
It's time to make things right and give them our support.

138
00:10:46,149 --> 00:10:46,669
Great.

139
00:10:46,769 --> 00:10:47,729
It's Neptune's army.

140
00:10:47,929 --> 00:10:48,869
Hey, no big deal.

141
00:10:48,969 --> 00:10:49,749
We can crush them.

142
00:10:50,009 --> 00:10:50,929
Kill them all.

143
00:10:50,949 --> 00:10:53,669
Stand tall and show these bastards what we're made of.

144
00:11:00,149 --> 00:11:02,149
Why the hell is a human fighting us?

145
00:11:05,809 --> 00:11:06,889
Move, slaves.

146
00:11:07,149 --> 00:11:07,449
Attack.

147
00:11:07,449 --> 00:11:11,149
Get out there and fight for us unless you want to die.

148
00:11:19,149 --> 00:11:21,069
Hum-o-hum-o-hum-o.

149
00:11:21,349 --> 00:11:21,929
Hurry up.

150
00:11:22,589 --> 00:11:23,909
March, slave tank.

151
00:11:24,129 --> 00:11:25,589
Turn right and head that way.

152
00:11:29,669 --> 00:11:30,149
Whoopsie.

153
00:11:30,149 --> 00:11:31,709
Worthless klutz.

154
00:11:31,709 --> 00:11:33,169
Just drag the bastard.

155
00:11:35,809 --> 00:11:37,869
Look at that pathetic flesh bag.

156
00:11:38,449 --> 00:11:39,109
Replace him.

157
00:11:39,229 --> 00:11:39,769
Come on.

158
00:11:40,569 --> 00:11:42,029
Come-o-hum-o-hum-o.

159
00:11:43,609 --> 00:11:45,209
That's truly disgusting.

160
00:11:45,849 --> 00:11:47,489
They all reek of hypocrisy.

161
00:11:48,449 --> 00:11:49,149
Nico Robin.

162
00:11:50,609 --> 00:11:53,449
Could you perhaps use your power to free those slaves?

163
00:11:53,949 --> 00:11:54,309
Really?

164
00:11:54,909 --> 00:11:55,969
Are you sure that's wise?

165
00:11:56,169 --> 00:11:57,449
They won't care for fishmen.

166
00:11:57,689 --> 00:12:00,829
I'll knock them unconscious if they try to take their grudge out on me.

167
00:12:01,089 --> 00:12:05,189
Because the life that they're living right now, they're even lower than beasts.

168
00:12:05,189 --> 00:12:08,749
This behavior was learned from the Celestial Dragons.

169
00:12:09,749 --> 00:12:11,209
I won't stand for it.

170
00:12:14,529 --> 00:12:15,369
All right.

171
00:12:15,689 --> 00:12:16,389
Count on me.

172
00:12:17,109 --> 00:12:17,749
Thank you.

173
00:12:21,709 --> 00:12:22,669
Let's go!

174
00:12:23,089 --> 00:12:24,849
Pick up the pace, you trash!

175
00:12:24,849 --> 00:12:27,849
Hum-o-hum-o-hum-o-hum-o.

176
00:12:27,849 --> 00:12:39,609
All our callers.

177
00:12:39,729 --> 00:12:40,549
They came off.

178
00:12:40,609 --> 00:12:40,849
Hey!

179
00:12:41,049 --> 00:12:41,989
What's the deal here?

180
00:12:42,289 --> 00:12:42,889
The hell?

181
00:12:43,269 --> 00:12:45,269
Who's taking the callers off of the slaves?

182
00:12:46,489 --> 00:12:47,309
Hey, woman.

183
00:12:47,549 --> 00:12:48,789
You're a straw hat, aren't you?

184
00:12:49,149 --> 00:12:51,189
Turn around and face me when I'm talking to you.

185
00:12:51,189 --> 00:12:52,029
Oh-oh-oh.

186
00:12:53,309 --> 00:12:55,809
What the hell is wrong with you worthless slaves?

187
00:12:56,009 --> 00:12:56,769
We're free.

188
00:12:57,049 --> 00:12:57,649
Was it you?

189
00:12:57,849 --> 00:13:00,049
Why save us when we were fighting against you?

190
00:13:00,629 --> 00:13:02,969
I can't say no to a handsome man.

191
00:13:03,549 --> 00:13:05,669
In other words, thank Boss Jinbei.

192
00:13:06,109 --> 00:13:06,669
Jinbei?

193
00:13:07,029 --> 00:13:07,869
But...

194
00:13:07,869 --> 00:13:08,869
How dare you!

195
00:13:09,369 --> 00:13:10,169
They're mine!

196
00:13:11,349 --> 00:13:12,089
Troll net!

197
00:13:15,089 --> 00:13:16,689
Hum-o-hum-o-hum-o-hum!

198
00:13:16,929 --> 00:13:18,429
Let's put you in chains!

199
00:13:24,709 --> 00:13:25,909
Web-o-fleur!

200
00:13:25,909 --> 00:13:26,909
What the hell?

201
00:13:26,909 --> 00:13:28,069
What the hell?

202
00:13:28,069 --> 00:13:29,369
This is getting weird!

203
00:13:33,909 --> 00:13:34,409
No!

204
00:13:34,789 --> 00:13:35,689
Cut that out!

205
00:13:36,209 --> 00:13:37,069
Just relax.

206
00:13:37,329 --> 00:13:38,449
This won't take long.

207
00:13:39,229 --> 00:13:40,109
Let go!

208
00:13:41,109 --> 00:13:41,849
Hang on!

209
00:13:42,009 --> 00:13:43,229
How are there two of you?

210
00:13:43,609 --> 00:13:43,849
A-ah!

211
00:13:44,109 --> 00:13:44,609
Double!

212
00:13:44,609 --> 00:13:53,069
She got Hammond!

213
00:13:53,069 --> 00:13:54,309
Will do, sir!

214
00:13:56,309 --> 00:13:58,069
Thanks a whole lot for the help, lady.

215
00:13:58,569 --> 00:14:00,809
You bastards treated us like trash.

216
00:14:00,809 --> 00:14:04,009
I'm gonna pay you back for every beating you gave me and then some.

217
00:14:04,009 --> 00:14:06,169
The enemy just freed all our slaves.

218
00:14:06,689 --> 00:14:07,929
It's a room of walls!

219
00:14:11,969 --> 00:14:12,329
No!

220
00:14:12,329 --> 00:14:12,529
No!

221
00:14:12,529 --> 00:14:12,789
No!

222
00:14:13,029 --> 00:14:13,609
No!

223
00:14:13,729 --> 00:14:14,229
Yes!

224
00:14:14,369 --> 00:14:14,689
Yes!

225
00:14:14,689 --> 00:14:14,989
No!

226
00:14:16,989 --> 00:14:21,929
Put-a-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put-put.

227
00:14:21,949 --> 00:14:22,969
Click.

228
00:14:22,969 --> 00:14:25,149
This is the border guard patrol calling, sir.

229
00:14:25,609 --> 00:14:27,329
Have I reached the minister of the left?

230
00:14:27,509 --> 00:14:27,949
You have?

231
00:14:28,169 --> 00:14:31,089
I've been frantically trying to call you over and over again.

232
00:14:31,169 --> 00:14:32,329
Why didn't you pick up?

233
00:14:32,349 --> 00:14:33,969
I don't mean to be insolent, sir.

234
00:14:34,389 --> 00:14:37,509
But I'm afraid there's no time for me to explain with our situation.

235
00:14:38,069 --> 00:14:39,809
Please, you need to warn the whole kingdom.

236
00:14:40,649 --> 00:14:41,589
It's the NOAA, sir.

237
00:14:41,989 --> 00:14:43,749
We've just been informed it's lost power.

238
00:14:44,169 --> 00:14:47,449
As a result, it's begun falling again, and it's hurtling towards the island.

239
00:14:50,969 --> 00:14:51,929
Surely not!

240
00:14:51,929 --> 00:14:53,929
What could this mean?

241
00:14:54,729 --> 00:14:56,029
Where are you calling from?

242
00:14:56,389 --> 00:14:58,369
The air tank, sir. From the control tower.

243
00:14:58,649 --> 00:15:02,649
That's good. That means you can warn everyone about the impending danger.

244
00:15:03,109 --> 00:15:05,409
All our communication centers are down.

245
00:15:06,009 --> 00:15:06,869
But you can help.

246
00:15:07,169 --> 00:15:11,389
You can contact the state-operated transponder snails all across the country.

247
00:15:11,809 --> 00:15:12,609
Please hurry.

248
00:15:12,929 --> 00:15:13,349
Yes, sir.

249
00:15:13,349 --> 00:15:23,469
This is an emergency announcement to all citizens of the Ryugu Kingdom.

250
00:15:24,029 --> 00:15:25,449
An evacuation has been issued.

251
00:15:25,909 --> 00:15:29,709
The giant ship, known as the NOAA, is falling towards Fishman Island.

252
00:15:30,829 --> 00:15:32,949
Everyone must flee the area immediately.

253
00:15:32,949 --> 00:15:52,389
I repeat, the NOAA is descending on the island.

254
00:15:52,849 --> 00:15:56,089
Everyone must flee immediately or face certain destruction.

255
00:15:56,089 --> 00:15:58,129
Is this for real?

256
00:15:58,849 --> 00:15:59,969
Look up there!

257
00:16:00,469 --> 00:16:02,609
The NOAA. You can see it.

258
00:16:03,209 --> 00:16:04,709
Is Deccan behind this?

259
00:16:05,349 --> 00:16:07,209
What? Are you really that surprised?

260
00:16:07,469 --> 00:16:09,029
That damn creepy stalker.

261
00:16:09,029 --> 00:16:11,049
I can't believe he would go this far.

262
00:16:11,229 --> 00:16:12,709
The bubble's gonna break!

263
00:16:12,829 --> 00:16:14,329
The island will be destroyed!

264
00:16:16,169 --> 00:16:18,509
Keep running. Just forget about your stuff.

265
00:16:19,089 --> 00:16:19,349
What?

266
00:16:19,889 --> 00:16:21,289
Get out of here! Quick!

267
00:16:24,589 --> 00:16:26,829
Everybody move it! The NOAA is coming!

268
00:16:28,229 --> 00:16:29,689
Did something bad happen?

269
00:16:29,849 --> 00:16:32,109
I heard the princess was drawing the ship away from the island.

270
00:16:32,369 --> 00:16:33,709
Yeah, I'm worried about her.

271
00:16:33,909 --> 00:16:35,929
We can't just swim off and abandon her now.

272
00:16:35,929 --> 00:16:39,429
What about the NOAA crashing into the island do you not get?

273
00:16:39,629 --> 00:16:40,549
I just...

274
00:16:40,549 --> 00:16:44,469
Do you guys really want to waste the princess's effort by staying here and dying?

275
00:16:45,489 --> 00:16:47,189
We have to leave the island!

276
00:16:47,649 --> 00:16:48,469
To the sea!

277
00:16:48,749 --> 00:16:49,889
Come on! Hurry!

278
00:16:51,169 --> 00:16:53,389
Oh, jeez. That thing's falling again?

279
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:53,669
Damn.

280
00:16:54,129 --> 00:16:55,769
You better fix this mess quick, Luffy.

281
00:16:56,589 --> 00:16:58,749
Something must have happened to Princess Shirohoshi.

282
00:16:59,449 --> 00:17:00,989
What's Deccan trying to pull?

283
00:17:01,169 --> 00:17:02,509
That crazy son of a bitch.

284
00:17:02,549 --> 00:17:03,929
We've got no choice but to run.

285
00:17:03,929 --> 00:17:05,529
That ship will kill us all.

286
00:17:05,929 --> 00:17:11,089
You can leave Horty and his associates to us.

287
00:17:11,429 --> 00:17:13,749
All of you citizens are ordered to flee the island.

288
00:17:14,089 --> 00:17:15,089
Now get going!

289
00:17:19,929 --> 00:17:21,009
What's wrong with you?

290
00:17:21,149 --> 00:17:21,909
I said go!

291
00:17:22,489 --> 00:17:23,429
No way!

292
00:17:24,929 --> 00:17:25,849
Wait. What?

293
00:17:27,369 --> 00:17:29,069
Women and children especially!

294
00:17:29,609 --> 00:17:30,769
Come on! Move it!

295
00:17:30,769 --> 00:17:32,189
We told you now!

296
00:17:32,589 --> 00:17:37,469
The Straw Hats may be a bunch of human pirates, but they're all down there fighting to save our island!

297
00:17:37,989 --> 00:17:41,389
We can't just run away and let them die when they're trying to help us!

298
00:17:41,429 --> 00:17:42,709
Uh... he's right.

299
00:17:43,089 --> 00:17:43,389
Hmm?

300
00:17:43,389 --> 00:17:46,509
We asked them to help us, and I'm not going to turn my back on them.

301
00:17:46,889 --> 00:17:50,269
I can't fight with them, but I won't leave them here to die and run away!

302
00:17:50,329 --> 00:17:50,989
Yes, exactly!

303
00:17:50,989 --> 00:17:52,729
It's the least we can do!

304
00:17:52,729 --> 00:17:53,229
Huh?

305
00:17:53,229 --> 00:17:54,229
Quiet!

306
00:17:54,229 --> 00:17:54,889
All of you!

307
00:17:56,149 --> 00:17:56,649
Listen up!

308
00:17:56,649 --> 00:17:58,189
I'm assigning you a duty.

309
00:17:58,609 --> 00:18:01,829
Tell every other spectator they need to evacuate right now!

310
00:18:01,949 --> 00:18:04,689
If you're going to stay, then save the others while you're here.

311
00:18:04,909 --> 00:18:05,609
Is that understood?

312
00:18:07,689 --> 00:18:10,329
I don't have time to argue with you about it.

313
00:18:10,549 --> 00:18:13,169
So if you want to stay behind, suit yourself!

314
00:18:17,869 --> 00:18:19,189
All right, outlaws!

315
00:18:19,569 --> 00:18:21,389
Time to face my wrath!

316
00:18:21,389 --> 00:18:29,269
Is this Straw Hat Luffy?

317
00:18:30,589 --> 00:18:32,849
All right, it's the air tank.

318
00:18:33,429 --> 00:18:35,009
We've met once before, remember?

319
00:18:36,689 --> 00:18:37,829
What is this?

320
00:18:38,369 --> 00:18:39,849
They're broadcasting to the pirates?

321
00:18:40,389 --> 00:18:41,589
We've heard everything.

322
00:18:42,049 --> 00:18:43,469
We are prepared to take action.

323
00:18:44,049 --> 00:18:47,249
We can see the Noah hurtling toward the island as we speak.

324
00:18:49,029 --> 00:18:49,949
Oh, Luffy!

325
00:18:49,949 --> 00:18:51,609
I don't know what to do!

326
00:18:52,249 --> 00:18:53,929
Do you hear those fools?

327
00:18:54,329 --> 00:18:57,829
They're broadcasting their conversation across the entire country!

328
00:18:58,429 --> 00:18:59,089
Hey, guys!

329
00:18:59,469 --> 00:19:01,649
What do we need to do to get a little air from you?

330
00:19:02,109 --> 00:19:04,389
We can shoot out all the air in the air tank.

331
00:19:04,949 --> 00:19:08,809
If we create a big bubble and shoot it, maybe it'll surround the Noah.

332
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:10,369
Shiro Hoshi!

333
00:19:11,069 --> 00:19:11,989
Straw Hat!

334
00:19:13,109 --> 00:19:14,749
I'm afraid that's all we can do.

335
00:19:15,029 --> 00:19:17,409
After we deploy the bubble, the rest is up to you.

336
00:19:17,609 --> 00:19:19,049
Don't make it more complicated!

337
00:19:19,049 --> 00:19:20,429
Just go for it, okay?

338
00:19:20,629 --> 00:19:21,649
Luffy's still all right.

339
00:19:22,169 --> 00:19:23,229
Thank goodness.

340
00:19:23,569 --> 00:19:25,309
He sounds as optimistic as ever.

341
00:19:25,569 --> 00:19:26,709
Hey, come on!

342
00:19:26,749 --> 00:19:28,089
It's Luffy we're talking about!

343
00:19:28,149 --> 00:19:29,269
I knew he'd be okay!

344
00:19:29,529 --> 00:19:30,969
I don't understand what's going on!

345
00:19:31,189 --> 00:19:32,169
What is he doing here?

346
00:19:32,389 --> 00:19:34,349
And more than that, what's the princess doing with him?

347
00:19:34,609 --> 00:19:36,949
Yeah, the Straw Hat guy's the one who kidnapped her, right?

348
00:19:37,429 --> 00:19:38,249
He's a human!

349
00:19:38,249 --> 00:19:43,529
And Luffy, everyone here is counting on you.

350
00:19:44,369 --> 00:19:48,589
Anyone else confused why the Border Guard's asking a human pirate to save the island?

351
00:19:49,049 --> 00:19:51,589
Hold on, does this mean that the human is on board the Noah?

352
00:19:51,909 --> 00:19:53,969
So is he trying to stop it?

353
00:19:53,969 --> 00:20:02,849
Can you hear me, Straw Hat?

354
00:20:03,849 --> 00:20:04,689
What?

355
00:20:05,429 --> 00:20:07,089
Prince Spook of Ocean?

356
00:20:07,089 --> 00:20:11,349
He spoke earlier and...

357
00:20:11,349 --> 00:20:14,669
It's clear now.

358
00:20:15,509 --> 00:20:16,729
Hordy is...

359
00:20:16,729 --> 00:20:31,389
Keep talking!

360
00:20:31,749 --> 00:20:33,589
Just tell us what Hordy is already!

361
00:20:43,769 --> 00:20:45,349
He's not a fish man.

362
00:20:45,349 --> 00:20:48,709
He's a monster brought to life by our hatred.

363
00:20:50,609 --> 00:20:51,669
Their hatred?

364
00:20:52,209 --> 00:20:53,669
What is he talking about?

365
00:20:54,609 --> 00:20:56,489
The new fish man pirates.

366
00:20:57,029 --> 00:21:00,209
They're nothing but remnants of a grudge from ages past.

367
00:21:04,869 --> 00:21:10,889
We allowed their evil to fester in the shadow of Fishman Island.

368
00:21:11,669 --> 00:21:14,789
And they began to champion this meaningless grudge.

369
00:21:15,349 --> 00:21:18,989
Flying its flag in some misguided sense of pride.

370
00:21:19,469 --> 00:21:21,229
They fear a future without it.

371
00:21:22,609 --> 00:21:25,369
In truth, they want humans to be evil.

372
00:21:25,929 --> 00:21:28,949
Otherwise, there is no reason to justify their crusade.

373
00:21:29,809 --> 00:21:32,109
All they desire is bloodshed.

374
00:21:33,409 --> 00:21:34,669
And despite what they say,

375
00:21:34,729 --> 00:21:36,529
they don't want peace for fish man either.

376
00:21:36,529 --> 00:21:49,229
Answer me, damn it!

377
00:21:49,569 --> 00:21:52,009
What did humans do to you that was so unforgivable?

378
00:21:53,609 --> 00:21:54,129
Why?

379
00:21:54,289 --> 00:21:56,709
What in this world could inspire such cruelty?

380
00:21:56,709 --> 00:22:04,689
That's not one damn thing?

381
00:22:04,889 --> 00:22:06,429
Hmm...

382
00:22:06,969 --> 00:22:08,769
Not one damn thing.

383
00:22:11,249 --> 00:22:12,029
That... that's your answer?

384
00:22:12,149 --> 00:22:12,669
Ugh!

385
00:22:13,249 --> 00:22:13,869
Uh...

386
00:22:14,129 --> 00:22:15,309
The simple truth.

387
00:22:15,309 --> 00:22:18,309
We were chosen by heaven to punish the humans.

388
00:22:19,309 --> 00:22:21,309
That's our purpose.

389
00:22:24,309 --> 00:22:27,309
And we have the power to do so.

390
00:22:30,309 --> 00:22:35,309
I understand now this sick and pathetic truth.

391
00:22:35,309 --> 00:22:48,309
All of their fury, their hatred, it doesn't come from experience or logic or fact.

392
00:22:51,309 --> 00:22:53,309
They have no substance.

393
00:22:57,309 --> 00:22:59,309
Just empty cruelty.

394
00:23:05,309 --> 00:23:12,309
Horty's hatred runs wild as Luffy continues to struggle in his undersea battle.

395
00:23:13,309 --> 00:23:16,309
A single shot of air fired from Fishman Island is Luffy's only hope.

396
00:23:17,309 --> 00:23:21,309
Yet even if the oxygen on the Noah is restored and Horty defeated, the ship itself could doom the island.

397
00:23:22,309 --> 00:23:26,309
Luffy vows to save the fishmen below, but their lives may never be the same.

